{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumUniverses.CategoricalConnection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumUniverses.CategoricalConnection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Pow.Real","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.ContinuousMap.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Geometry.Manifold.IsManifold.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.InnerProductSpace.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ModuleAction.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ModuleAction.unit","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L77-L77","doc":"**Unitality**: `ρ ∘ (η ⊗ id_V) = id_V` (up to left unitor). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ModuleAction.assoc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ModuleAction.assoc","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L74-L74","doc":"**Associativity**: `ρ ∘ (μ ⊗ id_V) = ρ ∘ (id_A ⊗ ρ)` up to associator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ModuleAction.action","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ModuleAction.action","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The action morphism `ρ : A ⊗ V → V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ModuleAction.target","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ModuleAction.target","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The object `V` acted upon. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ModuleAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ModuleAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.ModuleAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.ModuleAction","kind":"structure","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L61-L77","doc":"**Left module action** of a Frobenius–Hopf object `A` on another object `V`.\n\nA morphism `ρ : A ⊗ V → V` satisfying associativity and unitality,\ni.e. `V` is a left `A`-module in `C`.  (Auxiliary structure used in\nthe definition of the categorical action functional.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.leibniz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.leibniz","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L59-L59","doc":"**Leibniz rule**: `∇ ∘ μ = leibniz_rhs`, i.e. the connection is\na derivation with respect to the multiplication `μ`.\nThe full coherence diagram requires shuffling via the associator;\nstated here as an equality of morphisms `A ⊗ A → A ⊗ Ω¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.leibniz_rhs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.leibniz_rhs","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The Leibniz rule RHS: the categorical morphism `A ⊗ A → A ⊗ Ω¹`\nencoding `∇(a)·b + a·∇(b)`.  In a general (non-preadditive) monoidal\ncategory the \"sum\" cannot be expressed purely from `(∇, μ, α)`, so it\nis provided abstractly.  In a preadditive monoidal category this should\nbe `(∇ ▷ A) ≫ (α⁻¹) ≫ (μ ▷ Ω) + (A ◁ ∇) ≫ α ≫ …`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.nabla","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.nabla","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L48-L48","doc":"The connection morphism `∇ : A → A ⊗ Ω¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.Omega1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.Omega1","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L46-L46","doc":"The object of 1-forms `Ω¹` in `C`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection.mk","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalConnection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalConnection","kind":"structure","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.lean#L34-L59","doc":"**Categorical connection** on a Frobenius–Hopf object.\n\nA morphism `∇ : A → A ⊗ Ω¹` satisfying the Leibniz rule\n`∇(ab) = ∇(a) · b + a · ∇(b)`.  The object `Ω¹` represents the\nmodule of Kähler differentials in the categorical setting.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-connection}`\nRef: [kock2004] ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-connection","label":"def:categorical-connection","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-universes/categorical-connection.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}